    "field": "Paleoclimatology",
    "problem": "Understanding long-term climate dynamics and the relationship between orbital forcing, temperature, and greenhouse gases was challenging because direct ice core records were previously limited to only two glacial-interglacial cycles, hindering the analysis of recurring patterns and mechanisms over longer timescales.",
    "method": "This paper reconstructs the climate and atmospheric history of the past 420,000 years by analyzing deuterium, aerosols, and trapped greenhouse gases from a newly extended deep ice core recovered from Vostok station, Antarctica, to understand glacial-interglacial cycles and their drivers.",
    "task": "The task is to reconstruct the climate and atmospheric history of the past 420,000 years by analyzing atmospheric composition and climate properties from the Vostok ice core in Antarctica to understand past glacial-interglacial cycles and the correlation between greenhouse gases and temperature.",
